// The Dream, Test Beta 1.0: story logic (Yarn Spinner). The Prologue and Chapter 1 are Steven's script, in his words
// (the old game's dream/story.js scenes with the Unity game's Story.cs overrides). The acted scenes are films
// (story/SCRIPT.md); this decides which film plays, asks the choices in the game's UI, keeps the story variables, and
// holds the phone texts.
//   <<film id>>          play a rendered film and wait for it (Films/<id>.mp4)
//   <<money n "why">>    add to the bankroll
//   <<stake n>>          Slick lends n; half your profits go back until it's repaid
//   <<clock "11:20 PM">> the time on the phone's status bar
// Line tags: #text is a phone text from the speaker ("You" sends, to the contact in #to:<name>); #card heads the next
// choice and #hint explains the next option (in order); any other line is a narrator card on black.

title: Variables
---
// Variables the game sets before each run (game state, not saved here): $name (from the creator), $bankroll, $peak, $chapter (0 prologue,
// 1 Chapter 1), $room_title, and after an event $event, $won, $bust, $cooler, $qualified (made Day 2 of the Classic),
// $ft_end (the final-table film to play, or "") and $classic_end (who won Day 2 when you didn't).
<<declare $name = "">>
<<declare $bankroll = 0>>
<<declare $peak = 0>>
<<declare $chapter = 0>>
<<declare $room_title = false>>
<<declare $event = "">>
<<declare $won = false>>
<<declare $bust = false>>
<<declare $cooler = false>>
<<declare $qualified = false>>
<<declare $online = false>>
<<declare $classic_done = false>>
<<declare $ft_end = "">>
<<declare $classic_end = "">>
// Story variables (saved with the career): the job, the diner answer, and what has already been seen.
<<declare $job = "">>
<<declare $honest = false>>
<<declare $david_seen = false>>
<<declare $lesson_seen = false>>
<<declare $badbeat_seen = false>>
<<declare $firstwin_seen = false>>
<<declare $stake_seen = false>>
// the month (unity/docs/CH1_WEEKS.md): the calendar day (Mon 12 Jan = 7, the Classic Sat 14 Feb = 40), what you owe
// Slick, and each weekly beat once
<<declare $day = 0>>
<<declare $debt = 0>>
<<declare $debt_s = "">>
<<declare $wk2 = false>>
<<declare $wk3 = false>>
<<declare $wk3d = false>>
<<declare $wk4a = false>>
<<declare $wk4b = false>>
===

title: Prologue
---
// Monday, Floor 34; 2:13 AM at the Lucky Seven (the question, his answer); Saturday at the card room
<<film p_office>>
<<film p_diner>>
And what did you want to do? #card
-> Play poker. For real.
    <<set $honest to true>>
    <<film p_diner_yes>>
-> Doesn't matter now.
    <<set $honest to false>>
    <<film p_diner_no>>
<<film p_diner2>>
<<film p_seat>>
===

title: Monday
---
// After the Biscayne Championship: Monday at the office (no choice there any more), then Monday night at home, where
// Slick's text forces the decision (Story.cs p_after, p_offer, p_quit, p_keep)
<<film p_after>>
<<clock "11:20 PM">>
<<film p_offer>>
Slick: Saw your results from Saturday. Here's my offer. #text
Slick: Quit Lou. I'll put $2,000 in your account tomorrow. Not a loan. Don't make me regret it. #text
Slick: Or keep the job and play on the side. Your call, kid. It's the biggest one you'll make. #text
Decision time. #card
Slick's $2,000. One live game a day, any day. #hint
$2,000 saved, $1,250 every Friday. Live games on weekends. #hint
-> Quit. Text Lou tonight.
    <<set $job to "quit">>
    You: Lou. Redo it yourself. #text #to:Lou
    <<film p_quit>>
    <<money 2000 "Quit the 9-to-5. Slick's backing">>
    <<clock "11:31 PM">>
    Slick: Done. $2,000 is in your account. Not a loan. Don't make me regret it. #text
    Slick: Rent is due on the first. Never play above your roll. #text
    David: BRO. YOU QUIT YOUR JOB?? CALL ME #text
-> Keep the job. Grind nights and weekends.
    <<set $job to "nights">>
    <<money 2000 "Kept the day job. Savings">>
    <<film p_keep>>
    <<clock "11:48 PM">>
    Slick: Smart. A paycheck buys you time to learn. Never play above your roll. Text me when you win something. #text
<<film c1>>
===
